Subject: [PATCH 0/4] ACPI: SBS: Fix battery values on charge-limited batteries
To: "Rafael J. Wysocki" <rafael@kernel.org>,
    linux-acpi@vger.kernel.org
Cc: Len Brown <lenb@kernel.org>,
    Sebastian Reichel <sre@kernel.org>,
    linux-pm@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org


T2 Macs expose their battery through the ACPI Smart Battery System, and
with charge limits now set from user space, a few values reported by sbs
no longer match the battery:

- FullChargeCapacity and CycleCount are read once at probe, so
  charge_full keeps its boot value after the gauge learns a new one.
- capacity is AbsoluteStateOfCharge, which is relative to the design
  capacity instead of a full battery.
- A battery held at the charge limit is reported as full.
- Small discharge currents the gauge reports on AC switch the status to
  discharging, and user space shows a remaining time of several days.

The series was tested on a MacBookPro15,1 and a MacBookAir9,1, each with
a charge limit of 80 percent and with a full charge.

Andre Eikmeyer (4):
  ACPI: SBS: Read full charge capacity and cycle count with the state
  ACPI: SBS: Report the relative state of charge as capacity
  ACPI: SBS: Report full only when the battery is fully charged
  ACPI: SBS: Do not report discharging while on AC

 drivers/acpi/sbs.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

